inputs: sha256:1836a6f4cffcf3a40913e53d3bfeafc5d4fefb25e716136d3090fda86460e438
result: policy emitted
judge hosts kept out (T13): api.typesafe.ai, openrouter.ai
fragments:
  - protection (filesystem) backs config-tamper@4
  - judge-route (network) backs judge route (D-105)
  - task-allowlist (network) backs exfil-after-secrets@3
updates at the first prompt: none
absent:
  - path /library/application support/claudecode: not a Linux path: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /c/program files/claudecode: not a Linux path: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /home/agent/.claude/projects/*/memory: wildcard rule: Landlock paths are literal; its nearest listed ancestor decides
  - path /home/agent/.codex: codex configuration: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /home/agent/.config/opencode: opencode configuration: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /home/agent/.pi: pi configuration: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /home/agent/.config/jev-cops: jev-cops configuration: unlisted, inaccessible
  - path /home/agent/.jev-cops: the judge's private records and keys (D-098): unlisted, unreadable
  - default-branch-guard@2: no kernel equivalent: the pushed branch is inside the git-receive-pack body, not visible at L7; a deny_rules on git-receive-pack would block every push
  - off-repo-write@2: not deny-class (hold); the workspace read_write limit of the protection set bounds writes anyway
  - opaque-exec@1: not deny-class (at most hold); an opaque command has no deterministic target
  - tainted-destructive@1: no kernel equivalent: taint is not visible to the kernel or the proxy
  - model endpoints come from the attached provider profile (`_provider_*` rules, schema.mdx:116-117); the compiler never emits or removes them
gaps:
  - /home/agent/.claude.json stays writable (the harness rewrites it); config-tamper keeps it kill tier (D-107)
  - project config under the workspace stays writable (Landlock cannot carve read-only paths out of a read_write tree): /sandbox/.claude/hooks, /sandbox/.claude/settings.json, /sandbox/.claude/settings.local.json, /sandbox/.codex, /sandbox/.cops.toml, /sandbox/.opencode/plugin, /sandbox/.opencode/plugins, /sandbox/.pi/extensions, /sandbox/.pi/settings.json, /sandbox/opencode.json, /sandbox/opencode.jsonc; config-tamper keeps it kill tier, and Claude Code's hook is installed managed under /etc/claude-code
  - every process the agent starts shares the agent's network rules (network-rules.mdx:71-73): the task allowlist bounds where data can go, not which tool sends it
  - T13 is asserted on the base policy only: the gateway composes provider rules (`_provider_*`) into the effective policy, so a provider profile that allows a judge host (OpenRouter as both Pi's model provider and the judge) opens that route; check `policy get --full` (cops doctor, step 7)
refusals: none
diff against an empty policy:
  + rule jev_cops_judge
  + read_only /app
  + read_only /dev/urandom
  + read_only /etc
  + read_only /etc/claude-code
  + read_only /home/agent/.claude
  + read_only /home/agent/.claude/hooks
  + read_only /home/agent/.claude/plugins
  + read_only /home/agent/.claude/settings.json
  + read_only /home/agent/.claude/settings.local.json
  + read_only /lib
  + read_only /proc
  + read_only /usr
  + read_only /usr/local/libexec/jev-cops
  + read_only /var/log
  + read_write /dev/null
  + read_write /home/agent/.cache
  + read_write /home/agent/.claude.json
  + read_write /home/agent/.claude/plans
  + read_write /home/agent/.claude/projects
  + read_write /home/agent/.claude/todos
  + read_write /home/agent/.npm
  + read_write /sandbox
  + read_write /tmp
  ~ include_workdir
  ~ landlock
  ~ process
  note: filesystem, Landlock and process changes take effect only in a new sandbox (manage-policies.mdx:189-195)
exit 3
